Bluetooth: hci_sync: Don't double print name in add/remove adv_monitor

jira KERNEL-1078
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.126.1.el8_10
commit-author Douglas Anderson <dianders@chromium.org>
commit 6f55eea116ba3646fb5fbb31de703f8cf79d8214
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.126.1.el8_10/6f55eea1.failed

The hci_add_adv_monitor() hci_remove_adv_monitor() functions call
bt_dev_dbg() to print some debug statements. The bt_dev_dbg() macro
automatically adds in the device's name. That means that we shouldn't
include the name in the bt_dev_dbg() calls.

	Suggested-by: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.dentz@gmail.com>
	Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson <dianders@chromium.org>
	Signed-off-by: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6f55eea116ba3646fb5fbb31de703f8cf79d8214)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
diff --cc net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
